# Extensions

CarvePress has two extension layers: Carve engine extensions that render markup, and site extensions that subscribe to build events.

## Presets

|= Preset |= Included Carve engine factories |
| `minimal` | heading permalinks plus CarvePress code, compare, playground, images, and table scrolling |
| `docs` | `tabs`, `details`, `mathBlock`, `externalLinks`, `tocPlacement`, `wikilinks` |
| `full` | all `docs` factories plus `headingNumbers`, `glossary`, `index`, `citations`, `codeCallouts`, `colorSwatch`, `spoiler`, `listTable`, `imgFence`, `defaultAttributes` |

CarvePress always wraps the preset with Shiki, table scrolling, compare, playground, code groups, heading permalinks, and image defaults.

::: warning "Glossary ids changed with engine 0.1.10"
A glossary term keeps its case in its id, so `:: HTTP` renders `id="gloss-HTTP"` where engine 0.1.9 rendered `id="gloss-http"`. Two terms differing only in case used to collide and the second got no id at all; each now takes its own. Any `#gloss-...` deep link into a glossary on the `full` preset has to be respelled to match the term.
:::

## Site Extension Events

|= Event |= Payload |= Use |
| `buildStarted` | `{ config }` | Validate settings or capture normalized config. |
| `contentDiscovered` | `{ pages }` | Add virtual pages or filter pages. |
| `rendererCreated` | `{ extensions }` | Add Carve render extensions (see [Render Extensions][]). |
| `pageRendered` | `{ rendered, html }` | Post-process rendered HTML. |
| `pageWritten` | `{ rendered, outPath }` | Track emitted files. |
| `buildCompleted` | `{ rendered, outDir }` | Write derived artifacts. |

## Render Extensions

A render extension is a `PressExtension`: the extension bundle of Carve 0.2 (`extensions`, `renderers`, `transforms`), as each factory of `@markup-carve/carve/extensions` returns it, plus an optional `codeBlockRenderer`. Add one through `carve.extensions` or in a `rendererCreated` handler. A later entry replaces an earlier renderer of the same name, and an error a renderer throws fails the build.

```ts "carve-press.config.ts"
import { defineConfig } from '@markup-carve/carve-press'
import { glossary } from '@markup-carve/carve/extensions'

export default defineConfig({
  title: 'Docs',
  carve: { extensions: [glossary()] },
})
```

## Worked Example

```ts "site extension"
import type { SiteExtension } from '@markup-carve/carve-press'
import { writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises'
import { resolve } from 'node:path'

export function routeManifest(): SiteExtension {
  return {
    name: 'route-manifest',
    setup(bus) {
      bus.on('buildCompleted', async ({ rendered, outDir }) => {
        const routes = rendered.map((page) => page.searchDoc.route)
        await writeFile(resolve(outDir, 'routes.json'), JSON.stringify(routes, null, 2))
      }, 'route-manifest')
    },
  }
}
```

Built-in site extensions include `searchIndex`, `sitemap`, `llmsTxt`, `blog`, `feed`, and `redirects`.

